{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wheelgap/wheelgap/pulls/133","id":5228925430,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVnUUBc8AAAABN6sR9g","html_url":"https://github.com/wheelgap/wheelgap/pull/133","diff_url":"https://github.com/wheelgap/wheelgap/pull/133.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/wheelgap/wheelgap/pull/133.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wheelgap/wheelgap/issues/133","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wheelgap/wheelgap/pulls/133/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wheelgap/wheelgap/pulls/133/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wheelgap/wheelgap/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wheelgap/wheelgap/issues/133/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wheelgap/wheelgap/statuses/fdb892a93fbc26a9706e483d0ef78bef024d01cd","number":133,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix #114: --online looks up private-index lockfile packages on public PyPI","user":{"login":"Niranjan-cyber","id":177569959,"node_id":"U_kgDOCpWApw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177569959?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niranjan-cyber","html_url":"https://github.com/Niranjan-cyber","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niranjan-cyber/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niranjan-cyber/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niranjan-cyber/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niranjan-cyber/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niranjan-cyber/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niranjan-cyber/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niranjan-cyber/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niranjan-cyber/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niranjan-cyber/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #114\n\n**Problem:** --online looks up private-index lockfile packages on public PyPI\n\n**Cause:** The online index lookup ignores which index each lockfile package is pinned to. `fill_all` (used by --online) fetches every package from the default PyPI JSON API regardless of `Package.registry`, and `parse_poetry_lock` never records `registry` at all, so private-index packages get looked up on public PyPI.\n\n**Fix:** changes `src/wheelgap/cli.py` (+7 −1), `src/wheelgap/pypi.py` (+18 −4), `src/wheelgap/sources.py` (+3 −0).\n\n**Tests:** the new regression test `tests/test_patchpilot_issue_114.py::test_online_uv_lock_keeps_private_index_packages_off_pypi`, `tests/test_patchpilot_issue_114.py::test_online_poetry_lock_keeps_private_index_packages_off_pypi`, `tests/test_patchpilot_issue_114.py::test_parse_poetry_lock_records_registry` fails 2/2 on the original code (`33d640f`) and passes 2/2 with the fix in a fresh sandbox. 529 existing tests passed before and still pass. Repository checks run on the changed files: ruff check (no new problems), mypy (no new problems).\n\n**Limitations:** passing tests don't prove the change is bug-free; please review the logic. Not run here: ruff format; please check it in CI. The test doesn't claim to check: The same filtering rule as `recheck_lock()` is used, preferably via a shared helper.; A CHANGELOG entry is added under `## Unreleased` documenting the change..\n\n**AI assistance:** _This pull request was prepared with PatchPilot, an AI-assisted bug-fix tool. A human reviewed and approved this exact diff before it was opened. Please review it like any other contribution._\n\n<details><summary>More detail</summary>\n\n- Dependency check (SupplyGuard): no known-malicious packages; 0 known vulnerabilities listed.\n- Reviewer note (important): The issue requires a CHANGELOG entry under '## Unreleased', but the fix diff contains no CHANGELOG.md change.\n- Reviewer note (suggestion): The new shared helper is more permissive than the rule the issue specifies, changing recheck_lock() to also treat www.pypi.org, pypi.python.org, and files.pythonhosted.org as PyPI where it previously required exactly 'https://pypi.org/simple'.\n- Reviewer note (suggestion): Pushing the is_pypi filter into fill_all changes non---online behaviour too, since refresh=False calls would previously look up a private-index package with missing lock files on PyPI but now silently skip it.\n- Reviewer note (suggestion): The note assertion is weak: it only requires the substring 'index' and any standalone '1', so it can pass without verifying the actual count/other-index message wording.\n- Reviewer note (important): The test designer didn't claim its test checks 2 of the things the issue expects, so passing it may not prove the bug is fixed. Not claimed: The same filtering rule as `recheck_lock()` is used, preferably via a shared helper.; A CHANGELOG entry is added under `## Unreleased` documenting the change.\n- Base commit `33d640fca253addb35f1196abfe5f1ba20018806`; PatchPilot run e335ce16, revision 0.\n\n</details>","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-09T18:21:01Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T19:59:26Z","closed_at":"2026-11-09T19:58:56Z","merged_at":"2026-11-09T19:58:56Z","merge_commit_sha":"0c269c36631ae6effcfd4d18a039e634398a42e0","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"patrickballard","id":89168564,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MTY4NTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89168564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrickballard","html_url":"https://github.com/patrickballard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrickballard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrickballard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrickballard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrickballard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/user